window.NTI=window.NTI||{};(window.NTI.docs=window.NTI.docs||{})["kubernetes-19-higher-level-br-workloads"]={"html":"Higher-Level Workloads — Kubernetes Book 06\n\n\n<a href=\"#toc\">▤ TOC</a>\n\n\n<div class=\"page cover\">\n<div class=\"orb\"></div>\n<div class=\"orb\"></div>\n<div class=\"wheel\">🦾</div>\n<h1 id=\"higher-levelworkloads\">HIGHER-LEVEL<br />WORKLOADS</h1>\n<div class=\"sub\">Book 06 of the series — completing the workload zoo: DaemonSets (a Pod on every node), Jobs &amp; CronJobs (run-to-completion and schedules), StatefulSets in full (ordered lifecycle + partition canaries), and the autoscaling trio — HPA, VPA, Cluster Autoscaler.</div>\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"glass\">📡 DaemonSet<small>one Pod per node</small></div>\n<div class=\"glass\">⏳ Job<small>run to done</small></div>\n<div class=\"glass\">🗓️ CronJob<small>on a schedule</small></div>\n<div class=\"glass\">🪪 StatefulSet<small>full lifecycle</small></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"glass\">📈 HPA<small>more replicas</small></div>\n<div class=\"glass\">📏 VPA<small>bigger replicas</small></div>\n<div class=\"glass\">🖥️ Cluster Autoscaler<small>more nodes</small></div>\n<div class=\"glass\">🕊️ Canaries<small>partition updates</small></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ver\">K8S KNOWLEDGE BASE · BOOK 06 · CONTINUES BOOKS 01–05 · 2026</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<div class=\"page\">\n<div class=\"pghead\"><span class=\"chip\">📖</span><h2 id=\"contents-click-any-row\">Contents — click any row</h2><span class=\"dbadge\">6 parts · 19 chapters</span></div>\n<div class=\"tocgrid\">\n<div class=\"tocpart\">Part I · DaemonSets</div>\n<a href=\"#ch01\"><span class=\"cb\"></span><span class=\"tnum\">CH 01</span>DaemonSet — One Pod Per Node<span class=\"dots\"></span><span class=\"tp\">p.3</span></a>\n<a href=\"#ch02\"><span class=\"cb\"></span><span class=\"tnum\">CH 02</span>DaemonSet — Updates &amp; Node Lifecycle<span class=\"dots\"></span><span class=\"tp\">p.4</span></a>\n<div class=\"tocpart\">Part II · Jobs &amp; CronJobs</div>\n<a href=\"#ch03\"><span class=\"cb\"></span><span class=\"tnum\">CH 03</span>Jobs — Run to Completion<span class=\"dots\"></span><span class=\"tp\">p.5</span></a>\n<a href=\"#ch04\"><span class=\"cb\"></span><span class=\"tnum\">CH 04</span>CronJobs — Schedules &amp; Concurrency<span class=\"dots\"></span><span class=\"tp\">p.6</span></a>\n<div class=\"tocpart\">Part III · StatefulSets in Full</div>\n<a href=\"#ch05\"><span class=\"cb\"></span><span class=\"tnum\">CH 05</span>Ordered Lifecycle &amp; Stable Identity<span class=\"dots\"></span><span class=\"tp\">p.7</span></a>\n<a href=\"#ch06\"><span class=\"cb\"></span><span class=\"tnum\">CH 06</span>Update Strategies — Partition Canaries<span class=\"dots\"></span><span class=\"tp\">p.8</span></a>\n<div class=\"tocpart\">Part IV · Autoscaling</div>\n<a href=\"#ch07\"><span class=\"cb\"></span><span class=\"tnum\">CH 07</span>HPA — Horizontal Pod Autoscaler<span class=\"dots\"></span><span class=\"tp\">p.9</span></a>\n<a href=\"#ch08\"><span class=\"cb\"></span><span class=\"tnum\">CH 08</span>VPA — Vertical Autoscaler (Overview)<span class=\"dots\"></span><span class=\"tp\">p.10</span></a>\n<a href=\"#ch09\"><span class=\"cb\"></span><span class=\"tnum\">CH 09</span>Cluster Autoscaler — Nodes on Demand<span class=\"dots\"></span><span class=\"tp\">p.11</span></a>\n<a href=\"#ch10\"><span class=\"cb\"></span><span class=\"tnum\">CH 10</span>The Trio Together — When to Use Which<span class=\"dots\"></span><span class=\"tp\">p.12</span></a>\n<div class=\"tocpart\">Part V · Labs</div>\n<a href=\"#lab1\"><span class=\"cb\"></span><span class=\"tnum\">LAB 1</span>DaemonSet on Every Node<span class=\"dots\"></span><span class=\"tp\">p.13</span></a>\n<a href=\"#lab2\"><span class=\"cb\"></span><span class=\"tnum\">LAB 2</span>Jobs &amp; a Manual CronJob Trigger<span class=\"dots\"></span><span class=\"tp\">p.14</span></a>\n<a href=\"#lab3\"><span class=\"cb\"></span><span class=\"tnum\">LAB 3</span>HPA — Watch It Scale Under Load<span class=\"dots\"></span><span class=\"tp\">p.15</span></a>\n<a href=\"#lab4\"><span class=\"cb\"></span><span class=\"tnum\">LAB 4</span>StatefulSet Partition Canary<span class=\"dots\"></span><span class=\"tp\">p.16</span></a>\n<div class=\"tocpart\">Part VI · Prove It</div>\n<a href=\"#quiz\"><span class=\"cb\"></span><span class=\"tnum\">QUIZ</span>Self-Check Quiz<span class=\"dots\"></span><span class=\"tp\">p.17</span></a>\n<a href=\"#key\"><span class=\"cb\"></span><span class=\"tnum\">KEY</span>Answer Key + Scoring<span class=\"dots\"></span><span class=\"tp\">p.18</span></a>\n<a href=\"#gloss\"><span class=\"cb\"></span><span class=\"tnum\">GLOSS</span>Glossary<span class=\"dots\"></span><span class=\"tp\">p.19</span></a>\n<a href=\"#cheat\"><span class=\"cb\"></span><span class=\"tnum\">CHEAT</span>One-Page Cheat Sheet<span class=\"dots\"></span><span class=\"tp\">p.20</span></a>\n<a href=\"#finale\"><span class=\"cb\"></span><span class=\"tnum\">FINALE</span>Where to Next → Book 07<span class=\"dots\"></span><span class=\"tp\">p.21</span></a>\n</div>\n<div class=\"callout co-tip\"><span class=\"ico\">💡</span><div><b>Assumes Books 01–05.</b> You've already <i>met</i> everything here in passing: daemon-like agents skipped your drains (Book 04 · CH 10), Promtail/node-exporter ride DaemonSets (your observability stack!), and Book 05 built the StatefulSet storage half. This book finishes each story — then makes workloads <b>run themselves</b>.</div></div>\n<div class=\"pgfoot\"><span>📘 Book 06 · Higher-Level Workloads</span><span>◀ cover · start ▶</span><span>Page 2</span></div>\n</div>\n\n\n<div class=\"page\"><div class=\"pghead\"><span class=\"chip\">CH 01</span><h2 id=\"daemonset-one-pod-per-node\">📡 DaemonSet — One Pod Per Node</h2><span class=\"dbadge\">🟡 6 MIN · CORE</span></div>\n<p>A Deployment says <i>\"run N replicas, I don't care where.\"</i> A DaemonSet says <i>\"run exactly ONE Pod on EVERY node — new node joins, Pod spawns; node leaves, Pod vanishes.\"</i> Infrastructure agents live here.</p>\n<div class=\"zone zone-wk\">\n<div class=\"zlabel\">Deployment vs DaemonSet — the placement question</div>\n<div class=\"rowc\">\n<div class=\"kchip\">Deployment<small> \"3 total, anywhere\"</small></div><span class=\"harr\">⇄</span>\n<div class=\"kchip\">DaemonSet<small> \"1 per node, everywhere\"</small></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"rowc\">\n<div class=\"pod\">🫛 node1</div><div class=\"pod\">🫛 node2</div><div class=\"pod\">🫛 node3</div><span class=\"harr\">←</span><div class=\"nb c-teal\">📡 DaemonSet<small>every node, exactly one</small></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"term\"><span class=\"c\">apiVersion</span>: apps/v1\n<span class=\"c\">kind</span>: DaemonSet\n<span class=\"c\">metadata</span>: { <span class=\"c\">name</span>: log-agent }\n<span class=\"c\">spec</span>:\n  <span class=\"c\">selector</span>: { <span class=\"c\">matchLabels</span>: { <span class=\"c\">app</span>: log-agent } }\n  <span class=\"c\">template</span>:                       <span class=\"g\"># no `replicas:` field — the NODE LIST decides</span>\n    <span class=\"c\">metadata</span>: { <span class=\"c\">labels</span>: { <span class=\"c\">app</span>: log-agent } }\n    <span class=\"c\">spec</span>:\n      <span class=\"c\">containers</span>:\n      - <span class=\"c\">name</span>: agent\n        <span class=\"c\">image</span>: fluent/fluent-bit:2.2\n        <span class=\"c\">volumeMounts</span>:\n        - { <span class=\"c\">name</span>: logs, <span class=\"c\">mountPath</span>: <span class=\"m\">/var/log/pods</span>, <span class=\"c\">readOnly</span>: <span class=\"y\">true</span> }\n      <span class=\"c\">volumes</span>:\n      - <span class=\"c\">name</span>: logs\n        <span class=\"c\">hostPath</span>: { <span class=\"c\">path</span>: <span class=\"m\">/var/log/pods</span> }   <span class=\"g\"># node-local files (Book 05 · CH 02!)</span></div>\n<div class=\"table-scroll\"><table>\n<tr><th>The four classic tenants</th><th>Why per-node is mandatory</th></tr>\n<tr><td>📜 <b>Log collectors</b> — Fluent Bit, Promtail</td><td>container logs are files <b>on each node's disk</b> — only a local Pod can tail them (Book 01 · CH 03c logic)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>📈 <b>Metric agents</b> — node-exporter, Datadog agent</td><td>host metrics only exist at the node</td></tr>\n<tr><td>🌐 <b>Networking</b> — CNI plugins, kube-proxy</td><td>every node needs routing rules</td></tr>\n<tr><td>💾 <b>Storage</b> — CSI node plugins, Longhorn, GlusterFS</td><td>every node needs the mount machinery (Book 05 · CH 11!)</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"callout co-tip\"><span class=\"ico\">💡</span><div><b>You've been commanding DaemonSets for two books:</b> <code>drain --ignore-daemonsets</code> (Book 04 · CH 10) — their Pods are node-bound, so drain skips them. And your Loki stack's <b>Promtail runs as a DaemonSet</b> for exactly the /var/log/pods reason above.</div></div>\n<div class=\"callout co-key\"><span class=\"ico\">🔑</span><div><b>One sentence:</b> a DaemonSet is <i>\"infrastructure agents as YAML\"</i> — one Pod per node, born on join, gone on leave, no replicas field because <b>the node list IS the replica count</b>.</div></div>\n<p>⏭️ Updates, taints, and node churn — <a href=\"#ch02\">CH 02: DaemonSet Lifecycle</a></p>\n<div class=\"center\"><a href=\"#toc\">↑ back to top</a></div>\n<div class=\"pgfoot\"><span>📘 Book 06 · Higher-Level Workloads</span><span><a href=\"#toc\">▤ TOC</a> · <a href=\"#ch02\">next ▶</a></span><span>Page 3</span></div></div>\n\n\n<div class=\"page\"><div class=\"pghead\"><span class=\"chip\">CH 02</span><h2 id=\"daemonset-updates-amp-node-lifecycle\">🔄 DaemonSet — Updates &amp; Node Lifecycle</h2><span class=\"dbadge\">🟡 5 MIN</span></div>\n<h3 id=\"node-churn-the-automatic-part\">🆕 Node churn — the automatic part</h3>\n<div class=\"mtree\"><b>node4 joins</b>  <span class=\"g\">→ kubelet registers → DaemonSet controller notices →</span> <u>Pod spawns</u> <span class=\"p\">within seconds</span>\n<b>node4 dies</b>   <span class=\"g\">→ node object removed (or heartbeat lost) →</span> <u>Pod garbage-collected</u>\n<b>node tainted?</b> <span class=\"g\">→ DaemonSets auto-tolerate the <em>infrastructure</em> taints:</span>\n   <span class=\"g\">not-ready · unreachable · disk-pressure · memory-pressure</span> <span class=\"y\">✓ auto</span>\n   <span class=\"r\">control-plane:NoSchedule ✗ NOT auto</span> <span class=\"g\">— add the toleration yourself</span></div>\n<div class=\"term mini\"><span class=\"g\"># run your DS on control-plane nodes too (Book 04 · CH 05 taints, in action):</span>\n<span class=\"c\">tolerations</span>:\n- { <span class=\"c\">key</span>: node-role.kubernetes.io/control-plane, <span class=\"c\">operator</span>: <span class=\"y\">Exists</span>, <span class=\"c\">effect</span>: NoSchedule }</div>\n<h3 id=\"updatestrategy-rolling-your-agents\">🎞️ updateStrategy — rolling your agents</h3>\n<div class=\"table-scroll\"><table>\n<tr><th>Strategy</th><th>Behavior</th><th>Notes</th></tr>\n<tr><td><b>RollingUpdate</b> <span class=\"stbadge st-comp\">default</span></td><td>node by node, controlled by <code>maxUnavailable</code></td><td>no <code>maxSurge</code> for DaemonSets — agents replace in place, brief per-node gap is fine for infra</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>OnDelete</b></td><td>updated only when <i>you</i> delete each Pod</td><td>manual control for scary infrastructure (CNI!)</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"term mini\"><span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl set image ds/log-agent agent=fluent/fluent-bit:2.3\ndaemonset.apps/log-agent image updated\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl rollout status ds/log-agent\n<span class=\"p\">daemon set \"log-agent\" successfully rolled out</span></div>\n<ul>\n<li>🎛️ <b>nodeSelector / affinity respected:</b> add <code>nodeSelector: {gpu: \"true\"}</code> → the DaemonSet only covers GPU nodes — <i>\"one Pod per <b>matching</b> node\"</i> is the honest definition</li>\n<li>🗂️ <code>revisionHistoryLimit</code> keeps old controller revisions — <code>rollout undo</code> works on DaemonSets too</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"callout co-warn\"><span class=\"ico\">⚠️</span><div><b>Handle the control-plane exception:</b> forgetting the toleration above means your \"cluster-wide\" agent silently runs on <i>workers only</i> — and on single-node minikube (one control-plane node), it runs <b>nowhere</b>. Lab 1 rides this trap on purpose.</div></div>\n<div class=\"callout co-key\"><span class=\"ico\">🔑</span><div><b>One sentence:</b> DaemonSets ride the node lifecycle automatically — <i>join → spawn, leave → collect</i> — auto-tolerate infrastructure sickness but <b>not the control-plane taint</b>, and roll out node-by-node like Deployments minus the surge.</div></div>\n<p>⏭️ Workloads that END — <a href=\"#ch03\">CH 03: Jobs</a></p>\n<div class=\"center\"><a href=\"#toc\">↑ back to top</a></div>\n<div class=\"pgfoot\"><span>📘 Book 06 · Higher-Level Workloads</span><span><a href=\"#ch01\">◀ prev</a> · <a href=\"#toc\">▤ TOC</a> · <a href=\"#ch03\">next ▶</a></span><span>Page 4</span></div></div>\n\n\n<div class=\"page\"><div class=\"pghead\"><span class=\"chip\">CH 03</span><h2 id=\"jobs-run-to-completion\">⏳ Jobs — Run to Completion</h2><span class=\"dbadge\">🟡 6 MIN · CORE</span></div>\n<p>Everything so far runs <i>forever</i> — servers don't exit. A <b>Job</b> runs Pods to <b>completion</b>: migrate a schema, render a video, process yesterday's files. Success = exit 0. Then it stops.</p>\n<div class=\"term\"><span class=\"c\">apiVersion</span>: batch/v1\n<span class=\"c\">kind</span>: Job\n<span class=\"c\">metadata</span>: { <span class=\"c\">name</span>: nightly-etl }\n<span class=\"c\">spec</span>:\n  <span class=\"c\">completions</span>: <span class=\"y\">5</span>              <span class=\"g\"># run 5 SUCCESSFUL pods total</span>\n  <span class=\"c\">parallelism</span>: <span class=\"y\">2</span>              <span class=\"g\"># …but only 2 at a time</span>\n  <span class=\"c\">backoffLimit</span>: <span class=\"y\">4</span>              <span class=\"g\"># allow 4 failures before the JOB fails</span>\n  <span class=\"c\">activeDeadlineSeconds</span>: <span class=\"y\">3600</span>  <span class=\"g\"># hard wall-clock kill-switch</span>\n  <span class=\"c\">ttlSecondsAfterFinished</span>: <span class=\"y\">86400</span>  <span class=\"g\"># auto-cleanup 24h after done</span>\n  <span class=\"c\">template</span>:\n    <span class=\"c\">spec</span>:\n      <span class=\"c\">restartPolicy</span>: <span class=\"y\">Never</span>     <span class=\"g\"># OnFailure or Never — NEVER Always!</span>\n      <span class=\"c\">containers</span>:\n      - <span class=\"c\">name</span>: etl\n        <span class=\"c\">image</span>: myorg/etl:3.1</div>\n<div class=\"table-scroll\"><table>\n<tr><th>Field</th><th>Question it answers</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>completions</code> / <code>parallelism</code></td><td>how many successes total / how many concurrent — omitted → 1 and 1</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>backoffLimit</code></td><td>how many failed Pods before declaring the whole Job failed</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>activeDeadlineSeconds</code></td><td>when to give up regardless of retries</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>ttlSecondsAfterFinished</code></td><td>when the Job and its Pods clean themselves up</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>completionMode: Indexed</code></td><td>each Pod gets index <code>JOB_COMPLETION_INDEX</code> — sharding a work queue</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"term mini\"><span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl get job,pods -w\n<span class=\"y\">NAME            COMPLETIONS  DURATION  AGE</span>\nnightly-etl    2/5         45s       45s\n<span class=\"y\">NAME                STATUS    RESTARTS</span>\nnightly-etl-<span class=\"c\">abc</span>    <span class=\"p\">Running</span>   0\nnightly-etl-<span class=\"c\">def</span>    <span class=\"p\">Running</span>   0\nnightly-etl-<span class=\"c\">ghi</span>    <span class=\"stbadge st-comp\">Completed</span>  0  <span class=\"g\"># exit 0 — counts toward 5</span></div>\n<div class=\"callout co-warn\"><span class=\"ico\">⚠️</span><div><b>restartPolicy must be Never or OnFailure</b> — a Job template with <code>Always</code> is rejected. Think about it: a <i>completed</i> workload can't have an \"always restart\" policy. The Book 01 · CH 15 standalone-Pod problem also applies: a Job whose <b>node dies</b> gets its Pod recreated <i>by the Job controller</i> — a plain Pod wouldn't be.</div></div>\n<div class=\"callout co-key\"><span class=\"ico\">🔑</span><div><b>One sentence:</b> a Job is <i>a batch workload with an exit condition</i> — it counts <b>successes</b> (<code>completions</code>), bounds <b>failure</b> (<code>backoffLimit</code>), caps <b>time</b> (<code>activeDeadlineSeconds</code>), and cleans up after itself (<code>ttlSecondsAfterFinished</code>).</div></div>\n<p>⏭️ The same thing, on a clock — <a href=\"#ch04\">CH 04: CronJobs</a></p>\n<div class=\"center\"><a href=\"#toc\">↑ back to top</a></div>\n<div class=\"pgfoot\"><span>📘 Book 06 · Higher-Level Workloads</span><span><a href=\"#ch02\">◀ prev</a> · <a href=\"#toc\">▤ TOC</a> · <a href=\"#ch04\">next ▶</a></span><span>Page 5</span></div></div>\n\n\n<div class=\"page\"><div class=\"pghead\"><span class=\"chip\">CH 04</span><h2 id=\"cronjobs-schedules-amp-concurrency\">🗓️ CronJobs — Schedules &amp; Concurrency</h2><span class=\"dbadge\">🟡 6 MIN · CORE</span></div>\n<p>A CronJob creates a <b>Job on a schedule</b> — cron syntax you already know, wrapped around everything CH 03 taught.</p>\n<div class=\"term\"><span class=\"c\">apiVersion</span>: batch/v1\n<span class=\"c\">kind</span>: CronJob\n<span class=\"c\">metadata</span>: { <span class=\"c\">name</span>: db-backup }\n<span class=\"c\">spec</span>:\n  <span class=\"c\">schedule</span>: <span class=\"m\">\"30 2 * * *\"</span>          <span class=\"g\"># 02:30 daily (min hour dom month dow)</span>\n  <span class=\"c\">timeZone</span>: <span class=\"m\">\"Europe/Berlin\"</span>        <span class=\"g\"># stable zone — don't trust node clocks</span>\n  <span class=\"c\">concurrencyPolicy</span>: <span class=\"y\">Forbid</span>       <span class=\"g\"># ★ the policy that saves databases</span>\n  <span class=\"c\">startingDeadlineSeconds</span>: <span class=\"y\">300</span>    <span class=\"g\"># missed &gt; 5 min ago → skip, don't stampede</span>\n  <span class=\"c\">suspend</span>: <span class=\"y\">false</span>                   <span class=\"g\"># true = pause the schedule, keep the object</span>\n  <span class=\"c\">successfulJobsHistoryLimit</span>: <span class=\"y\">3</span>\n  <span class=\"c\">failedJobsHistoryLimit</span>: <span class=\"y\">1</span>\n  <span class=\"c\">jobTemplate</span>:                     <span class=\"g\"># ← everything from CH 03 lives in here</span>\n    <span class=\"c\">spec</span>:\n      <span class=\"c\">backoffLimit</span>: <span class=\"y\">2</span>\n      <span class=\"c\">template</span>:\n        <span class=\"c\">spec</span>:\n          <span class=\"c\">restartPolicy</span>: Never\n          <span class=\"c\">containers</span>:\n          - <span class=\"c\">name</span>: dump\n            <span class=\"c\">image</span>: postgres:16\n            <span class=\"c\">command</span>: [<span class=\"m\">pg_dump</span>, <span class=\"m\">-f</span>, <span class=\"m\">/backup/dump.sql</span>, <span class=\"m\">$DATABASE_URL</span>]</div>\n<div class=\"table-scroll\"><table>\n<tr><th>concurrencyPolicy</th><th>If the previous run is still going…</th><th>Use for</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>Allow</code> <span class=\"stbadge st-comp\">default</span></td><td>start another anyway — runs overlap</td><td>idempotent jobs (cache warmers)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>Forbid</code></td><td><b>skip</b> this tick</td><td>backups, billing — two overlapping runs = disaster</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>Replace</code></td><td><b>kill</b> the old run, start new</td><td>\"latest state wins\" jobs</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"callout co-warn\"><span class=\"ico\">⚠️</span><div><b>The overlap trap:</b> a backup that takes 25 min on a 15-min schedule, with <code>Allow</code>, silently runs <i>two backups against the same database</i>. <code>Forbid</code> is the professional default for anything touching shared state — and <code>startingDeadlineSeconds</code> prevents a recovered controller from firing 47 missed ticks at once.</div></div>\n<div class=\"term mini\"><span class=\"g\"># fire a schedule right now — the tester's cheat code:</span>\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl create job backup-test <span class=\"y\">--from</span>=cronjob/db-backup\njob.batch/backup-test created\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl get jobs  <span class=\"g\"># backup-test 0/1 → 1/1 — full CH 03 machinery</span></div>\n<div class=\"callout co-key\"><span class=\"ico\">🔑</span><div><b>One sentence:</b> a CronJob = <b>cron schedule + Job template + a concurrency policy</b> — and the entire craft is choosing <code>Allow/Forbid/Replace</code> correctly, because overlapping batch runs are where data gets hurt.</div></div>\n<p>⏭️ Part III: the cattle-and-names workload, in full — <a href=\"#ch05\">CH 05: StatefulSets</a></p>\n<div class=\"center\"><a href=\"#toc\">↑ back to top</a></div>\n<div class=\"pgfoot\"><span>📘 Book 06 · Higher-Level Workloads</span><span><a href=\"#ch03\">◀ prev</a> · <a href=\"#toc\">▤ TOC</a> · <a href=\"#ch05\">next ▶</a></span><span>Page 6</span></div></div>\n\n\n<div class=\"page\"><div class=\"pghead\"><span class=\"chip\">CH 05</span><h2 id=\"statefulsets-ordered-lifecycle-amp-identity\">🪪 StatefulSets — Ordered Lifecycle &amp; Identity</h2><span class=\"dbadge\">🟡 6 MIN · CORE</span></div>\n<p>Book 05 gave StatefulSets their storage (<code>volumeClaimTemplates</code>, per-replica claims). This page completes the other half: <b>ordered lifecycle</b> and <b>stable identity</b> — the two things a replica set of a database can't live without.</p>\n<div class=\"mtree\"><b>StatefulSet db · replicas: 3</b>\n<span class=\"g\">SCALE UP (ordered):</span>\n  db-<b>0</b> created → <u>waits for Running &amp; Ready</u> → db-<b>1</b> → … → db-<b>2</b>\n<span class=\"g\">SCALE DOWN (reverse):</span>\n  db-<b>2</b> deleted first → then db-<b>1</b> → db-<b>0</b> last  <span class=\"g\">(primary dies last!)</span>\n<span class=\"g\">DELETION of the STS:</span> same reverse order — and claims SURVIVE (Book 05 · CH 10)</div>\n<div class=\"grid2\">\n<div class=\"card\">\n<div class=\"zlabel\">Stable network identity</div>\n<div class=\"term mini\"><span class=\"g\"># via the HEADLESS svc (Book 05 · CH 09):</span>\ndb-<b>0</b>.db.shop.svc.cluster.local\ndb-<b>1</b>.db.shop.svc.cluster.local\ndb-<b>2</b>.db.shop.svc.cluster.local\n<span class=\"g\"># names survive rescheduling —\n# \"follow db-0\" is a TRUE forever</span></div></div>\n<div class=\"card\">\n<div class=\"zlabel\">podManagementPolicy</div>\n<div class=\"term mini\"><span class=\"y\">OrderedReady</span> <span class=\"g\">(default)</span>\n<span class=\"g\">strict sequence, wait-for-Ready —\ncorrect for most databases</span>\n<span class=\"y\">Parallel</span>\n<span class=\"g\">spawn/kill all at once — for\npeers that self-coordinate\n(e.g. some distributed DBs)</span></div></div>\n</div>\n<ul>\n<li>🐣 <b>Why ordered matters:</b> a primary must be <i>Ready</i> before followers attach to it — Parallel would race followers against a half-booted primary</li>\n<li>🔁 <b>Re-created in place:</b> kill db-1 → the <b>same name</b> returns, reattaches <code>data-db-1</code> (Book 05 · Lab 3 proved the data comes back) — the identity is the contract</li>\n<li>🪢 <b>Cascade control:</b> <code>kubectl delete sts db --cascade=orphan</code> leaves the Pods running — hand-migrate them, then adopt</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"callout co-key\"><span class=\"ico\">🔑</span><div><b>One sentence:</b> StatefulSets = <b>ordered birth/reverse-order death + wait-for-Ready between steps + names and DNS that never change</b> — storage (Book 05) plus sequence plus identity, the full definition of \"stateful.\"</div></div>\n<p>⏭️ Updating these delicate creatures safely — <a href=\"#ch06\">CH 06: Partition Canaries</a></p>\n<div class=\"center\"><a href=\"#toc\">↑ back to top</a></div>\n<div class=\"pgfoot\"><span>📘 Book 06 · Higher-Level Workloads</span><span><a href=\"#ch04\">◀ prev</a> · <a href=\"#toc\">▤ TOC</a> · <a href=\"#ch06\">next ▶</a></span><span>Page 7</span></div></div>\n\n\n<div class=\"page\"><div class=\"pghead\"><span class=\"chip\">CH 06</span><h2 id=\"statefulset-updates-partition-canaries\">🕊️ StatefulSet Updates — Partition Canaries</h2><span class=\"dbadge\">🟡 6 MIN · CORE</span></div>\n<p>Rolling a database's image is scarier than rolling nginx. StatefulSets answer with <b>partitioned rollouts</b>: update a controlled slice first, verify, then let it finish.</p>\n<div class=\"term\"><span class=\"c\">spec</span>:\n  <span class=\"c\">updateStrategy</span>:\n    <span class=\"c\">type</span>: <span class=\"y\">RollingUpdate</span>          <span class=\"g\"># or: OnDelete (manual, like DaemonSets)</span>\n    <span class=\"c\">rollingUpdate</span>:\n      <span class=\"c\">partition</span>: <span class=\"y\">2</span>               <span class=\"g\"># ONLY pods with ordinal ≥ 2 update</span></div>\n<div class=\"zone zone-cp\">\n<div class=\"zlabel\">partition: 2 on a 3-replica StatefulSet — after <code>set image</code></div>\n<div class=\"rowc\">\n<div class=\"nb c-slate\">db-0<small>postgres:16 · <b>old</b></small></div>\n<div class=\"nb c-slate\">db-1<small>postgres:16 · <b>old</b></small></div>\n<div class=\"nb c-emerald\">db-2<small>postgres:<b>17</b> · NEW 🕊️</small></div>\n</div>\n<p>the canary flies solo — verify it, then lower the partition to release the rest</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"term mini\"><span class=\"g\"># the canary release, step by step:</span>\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl patch sts db <span class=\"y\">--type</span>=merge <span class=\"y\">-p</span> \\\n  <span class=\"m\">'{\"spec\":{\"updateStrategy\":{\"rollingUpdate\":{\"partition\":2}}}}'</span>\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl set image sts/db db=postgres:<span class=\"y\">17</span>\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl get pod db-2 -o jsonpath=<span class=\"m\">'{.spec.containers[0].image}'</span>\npostgres:<span class=\"y\">17</span>   <span class=\"g\"># db-0/db-1 untouched ✓</span>\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> <span class=\"g\"># …run your checks against db-2… then release:</span>\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl patch sts db <span class=\"y\">--type</span>=merge <span class=\"y\">-p</span> \\\n  <span class=\"m\">'{\"spec\":{\"updateStrategy\":{\"rollingUpdate\":{\"partition\":0}}}}'</span>\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl get pods -w\n<span class=\"y\">db-2  1/1  Running  <span class=\"g\">(already new)</span></span>\n<span class=\"y\">db-1  0/1  Terminating  → 1/1 <span class=\"g\">on :17</span></span>  <span class=\"g\"># highest ordinal first!</span>\n<span class=\"y\">db-0  0/1  Terminating  → 1/1 <span class=\"g\">on :17</span></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li>🔻 <b>Roll direction is highest-ordinal-first</b> — replicas (followers) update before the primary (db-0). Followers run the new version against the old primary — the safe direction for replication compat</li>\n<li>🕊️ <code>partition = replicas</code> → <b>nothing updates</b> (freeze). Lower gradually: 2 → 1 → 0</li>\n<li>✋ <b>OnDelete</b> — full manual: delete each Pod yourself to pull the new template (CNI/CSI-adjacent caution)</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"callout co-tip\"><span class=\"ico\">💡</span><div><b>Compare to Deployments:</b> Deployments have <code>maxUnavailable/maxSurge</code> (Book 01 · CH 20) — availability control. StatefulSets have <code>partition</code> — <b>blast-radius control</b>. One Pod at a time, ordered, canary-able: exactly what replicas of a database deserve.</div></div>\n<div class=\"callout co-key\"><span class=\"ico\">🔑</span><div><b>One sentence:</b> <code>partition</code> turns a StatefulSet rollout into a <b>graduated canary from the top down</b> — verify one replica on the new version before you let the primary anywhere near it.</div></div>\n<p>⏭️ Part IV: workloads that resize themselves — <a href=\"#ch07\">CH 07: HPA</a></p>\n<div class=\"center\"><a href=\"#toc\">↑ back to top</a></div>\n<div class=\"pgfoot\"><span>📘 Book 06 · Higher-Level Workloads</span><span><a href=\"#ch05\">◀ prev</a> · <a href=\"#toc\">▤ TOC</a> · <a href=\"#ch07\">next ▶</a></span><span>Page 8</span></div></div>\n\n\n<div class=\"page\"><div class=\"pghead\"><span class=\"chip\">CH 07</span><h2 id=\"hpa-horizontal-pod-autoscaler\">📈 HPA — Horizontal Pod Autoscaler</h2><span class=\"dbadge\">🟡 6 MIN · CORE</span></div>\n<p>The HPA watches a metric and edits <code>spec.replicas</code> for you — <b>more copies under load, fewer when quiet</b>. One controller, one loop (Book 01's reconciliation, aimed at sizing).</p>\n<div class=\"term\"><span class=\"c\">apiVersion</span>: autoscaling/v2\n<span class=\"c\">kind</span>: HorizontalPodAutoscaler\n<span class=\"c\">metadata</span>: { <span class=\"c\">name</span>: web-hpa }\n<span class=\"c\">spec</span>:\n  <span class=\"c\">scaleTargetRef</span>:\n    { <span class=\"c\">apiVersion</span>: apps/v1, <span class=\"c\">kind</span>: Deployment, <span class=\"c\">name</span>: web }\n  <span class=\"c\">minReplicas</span>: <span class=\"y\">2</span>                 <span class=\"g\"># floor — never below (HA!)</span>\n  <span class=\"c\">maxReplicas</span>: <span class=\"y\">10</span>                <span class=\"g\"># ceiling — your wallet's guard rail</span>\n  <span class=\"c\">metrics</span>:\n  - <span class=\"c\">type</span>: Resource\n    <span class=\"c\">resource</span>:\n      <span class=\"c\">name</span>: cpu\n      <span class=\"c\">target</span>: { <span class=\"c\">type</span>: <span class=\"y\">Utilization</span>, <span class=\"c\">averageUtilization</span>: <span class=\"y\">60</span> }\n      <span class=\"g\"># \"keep average CPU at 60% OF EACH POD'S REQUEST\"</span></div>\n<div class=\"callout co-warn\"><span class=\"ico\">⚠️</span><div><b>HPA needs <code>requests</code> set (Book 02 · CH 14).</b> Utilization = <i>actual usage ÷ request</i> — no request means no denominator, and the HPA sits <span class=\"stbadge st-pend\">unknown</span>. It also needs the <b>metrics-server</b> installed (<code>minikube addons enable metrics-server</code>) — the component that aggregates real usage.</div></div>\n<h3 id=\"the-math-it-s-one-formula\">🧮 The math (it's one formula)</h3>\n<div class=\"mtree\"><b>desiredReplicas = ceil[ currentReplicas × (currentMetric ÷ targetMetric) ]</b>\n<span class=\"g\">4 pods at 90% CPU, target 60%:</span>  ceil(4 × 90/60) = <span class=\"p\">6 pods</span>\n<span class=\"g\">2 pods at 15%, target 60%:</span>    ceil(2 × 15/60) = <span class=\"p\">1 pod</span>\n<span class=\"g\">…but within a ±10% tolerance band — no flapping on noise.\n…always clamped to [minReplicas, maxReplicas].</span></div>\n<ul>\n<li>⏱️ <b>Asymmetric by design:</b> check every ~15s; <b>scale-up is fast</b>, <b>scale-down waits</b> (default stabilization window 5 min) — traffic spikes shouldn't mass-terminate Pods they may need again</li>\n<li>📊 <b>Metric sources:</b> <code>Resource</code> (cpu/memory per-pod) · <code>Pods</code> (custom per-pod: requests/sec) · <code>External</code> (queue depth, cloud LB RPS)</li>\n<li>🚫 Scale targets: Deployment, ReplicaSet, StatefulSet — <b>not</b> DaemonSets (node-bound by definition)</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"callout co-key\"><span class=\"ico\">🔑</span><div><b>One sentence:</b> the HPA is a <b>replica thermostat</b> — it divides observed load by your <code>requests</code>-based target and scales within your min/max rails, fast up, slow down. Lab 3 makes the needle move in front of you.</div></div>\n<p>⏭️ Scaling a different axis — <a href=\"#ch08\">CH 08: VPA</a></p>\n<div class=\"center\"><a href=\"#toc\">↑ back to top</a></div>\n<div class=\"pgfoot\"><span>📘 Book 06 · Higher-Level Workloads</span><span><a href=\"#ch06\">◀ prev</a> · <a href=\"#toc\">▤ TOC</a> · <a href=\"#ch08\">next ▶</a></span><span>Page 9</span></div></div>\n\n\n<div class=\"page\"><div class=\"pghead\"><span class=\"chip\">CH 08</span><h2 id=\"vpa-vertical-autoscaler-overview\">📏 VPA — Vertical Autoscaler (Overview)</h2><span class=\"dbadge\">🔵 OVERVIEW</span></div>\n<p>The HPA answers <i>\"wrong NUMBER of copies.\"</i> The VPA answers <i>\"wrong SIZE of copy\"</i> — it watches actual usage and adjusts each Pod's <b>requests/limits</b> (Book 02 · CH 14).</p>\n<div class=\"grid2\">\n<div class=\"card\"><div class=\"zlabel\">Horizontal (HPA)</div>\n<div class=\"mtree\">🫛 🫛 🫛  <span class=\"g\">→ load →</span>  🫛 🫛 🫛 🫛 🫛 🫛\n<span class=\"g\">same size, more of them</span></div></div>\n<div class=\"card\"><div class=\"zlabel\">Vertical (VPA)</div>\n<div class=\"mtree\">🫛(200m)  <span class=\"g\">→ load →</span>  🫛(500m)\n<span class=\"g\">same count, bigger each</span></div></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"term mini\"><span class=\"g\"># the VPA object — installed separately (CRDs + recommender component):</span>\n<span class=\"c\">apiVersion</span>: autoscaling.k8s.io/v1\n<span class=\"c\">kind</span>: VerticalPodAutoscaler\n<span class=\"c\">metadata</span>: { <span class=\"c\">name</span>: web-vpa }\n<span class=\"c\">spec</span>:\n  <span class=\"c\">targetRef</span>: { <span class=\"c\">apiVersion</span>: apps/v1, <span class=\"c\">kind</span>: Deployment, <span class=\"c\">name</span>: web }\n  <span class=\"c\">updatePolicy</span>:\n    <span class=\"c\">updateMode</span>: <span class=\"y\">Auto</span>      <span class=\"g\"># Off | Initial | Recreate (Auto)</span></div>\n<div class=\"table-scroll\"><table>\n<tr><th>Mode</th><th>Behavior</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>Off</code></td><td><b>recommendations only</b> — the right starting point: read <code>kubectl describe vpa</code>, tune your YAML yourself</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>Initial</code></td><td>apply recommended requests only to <b>newly created</b> Pods — no disruption</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>Auto</code> / <code>Recreate</code></td><td><b>evicts</b> Pods to apply new sizes (Book 01's eviction, by an autoscaler this time)</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"callout co-warn\"><span class=\"ico\">⚠️</span><div><b>The classic conflict:</b> HPA on <b>cpu</b> + VPA on <b>cpu</b> = a feedback fight (VPA raises requests → utilization % falls → HPA scales down…). Allowed combo: <b>HPA on custom/external metrics + VPA on cpu/memory</b> — different signals, no loop. This is also why \"just install everything\" autoscaling is a mistake.</div></div>\n<div class=\"callout co-key\"><span class=\"ico\">🔑</span><div><b>One sentence:</b> the VPA is a <b>right-sizing engine</b> — same knob as Book 02's requests/limits, turned automatically; start in <code>Off</code> mode and treat its recommendations as the end of guesswork, not as an autopilot.</div></div>\n<p>⏭️ And when the NODES run out — <a href=\"#ch09\">CH 09: Cluster Autoscaler</a></p>\n<div class=\"center\"><a href=\"#toc\">↑ back to top</a></div>\n<div class=\"pgfoot\"><span>📘 Book 06 · Higher-Level Workloads</span><span><a href=\"#ch07\">◀ prev</a> · <a href=\"#toc\">▤ TOC</a> · <a href=\"#ch09\">next ▶</a></span><span>Page 10</span></div></div>\n\n\n<div class=\"page\"><div class=\"pghead\"><span class=\"chip\">CH 09</span><h2 id=\"cluster-autoscaler-nodes-on-demand\">🖥️ Cluster Autoscaler — Nodes on Demand</h2><span class=\"dbadge\">🔵 OVERVIEW</span></div>\n<p>HPA and VPA resize <i>within</i> the cluster's capacity. The <b>Cluster Autoscaler (CA)</b> resizes the capacity itself — adding and removing <b>nodes</b>, driven by two signals:</p>\n<div class=\"mtree\"><b>SCALE UP trigger:</b>  Pods stuck <span class=\"r\">Pending</span> <span class=\"g\">— Book 04's funnel found NO feasible node —\n                    (requests don't fit / taints / affinity)</span>\n      <span class=\"g\">CA asks the cloud provider (node group / ASG / MIG) for one more node →\n      node joins → those Pending pods schedule ✓</span>\n\n<b>SCALE DOWN trigger:</b> a node is <span class=\"y\">underutilized ~10+ min</span> AND every Pod on it\n      <span class=\"g\">can be safely rescheduled onto other nodes → drain-style eviction →\n      node removed → bill shrinks ✓</span></div>\n<div class=\"table-scroll\"><table>\n<tr><th>Pods CA will NOT evict (block scale-down)</th><th>Why</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Pods under a restrictive <b>PDB</b> (Book 04 · CH 10)</td><td>voluntary-disruption protection is honored</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Pods with <b>local storage</b> (emptyDir/hostPath) — unless <code>cluster-autoscaler.kubernetes.io/safe-to-evict: \"true\"</code></td><td>eviction = data loss (Book 05 · CH 02!)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>High-priority</b> / system Pods (Book 04 · CH 09)</td><td>pecking order respected</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Pods the controller wouldn't recreate elsewhere (anti-affinity pinned, standalone)</td><td>they'd strand</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"callout co-tip\"><span class=\"ico\">💡</span><div><b>Configuration is per cloud, per node group:</b> you annotate/label node groups with <code>min</code>/<code>max</code> sizes and deploy the CA with your provider's flags — it's cloud-native by design. <b>On minikube it doesn't function</b> (no expandable node group behind it) — this is a production-environment component, which is why this chapter is an overview.</div></div>\n<div class=\"callout co-key\"><span class=\"ico\">🔑</span><div><b>One sentence:</b> the CA is <b>node-count automation</b> — Pending Pods are its \"buy more\" signal, idle nodes its \"sell some\" signal, and PDBs/local-storage/priority are the fences it will never jump (Book 04's safety rules, enforced by an accountant).</div></div>\n<p>⏭️ Three scalers, one stack — <a href=\"#ch10\">CH 10: The Trio Together</a></p>\n<div class=\"center\"><a href=\"#toc\">↑ back to top</a></div>\n<div class=\"pgfoot\"><span>📘 Book 06 · Higher-Level Workloads</span><span><a href=\"#ch08\">◀ prev</a> · <a href=\"#toc\">▤ TOC</a> · <a href=\"#ch10\">next ▶</a></span><span>Page 11</span></div></div>\n\n\n<div class=\"page\"><div class=\"pghead\"><span class=\"chip\">CH 10</span><h2 id=\"the-trio-together-when-to-use-which\">🧩 The Trio Together — When to Use Which</h2><span class=\"dbadge\">🔵 REFERENCE</span></div>\n<p>Three autoscalers, three <b>different questions</b>. Confusing them is how clusters get expensive or fall over.</p>\n<div class=\"table-scroll\"><table>\n<tr><th></th><th>📈 HPA</th><th>📏 VPA</th><th>🖥️ Cluster Autoscaler</th></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Question</b></td><td>how many copies?</td><td>how big is a copy?</td><td>how many nodes?</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Adjusts</b></td><td><code>spec.replicas</code></td><td>requests/limits (via eviction)</td><td>node-group size (cloud)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Signal</b></td><td>cpu/mem utilization, custom metrics</td><td>observed usage history</td><td>Pending Pods / idle nodes</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Layer</b></td><td>Pods</td><td>Pods</td><td>Nodes</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Latency</b></td><td>~15 s checks</td><td>recommend + evict (minutes)</td><td>minutes (cloud API)</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<h3 id=\"how-they-stack-the-beautiful-part\">🏗️ How they stack (the beautiful part)</h3>\n<div class=\"zone zone-wk\">\n<div class=\"rowc\">\n<div class=\"nb c-amber\">📈 HPA<small>replicas 3 → 9 under load</small></div>\n<span class=\"harr\">──►</span>\n<div class=\"kchip\">no node fits the new Pods → <span class=\"r\">Pending</span></div>\n<span class=\"harr\">──►</span>\n<div class=\"nb c-slate\">🖥️ CA<small>adds a node → Pending clears</small></div>\n</div>\n<p>HPA creates the demand · CA creates the room — they compose by design; VPA right-sizes underneath (on different metrics!)</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"grid3\">\n<div class=\"card center\"><p><b>Traffic-shaped load?</b><br />→ HPA (resource or custom metric)</p></div>\n<div class=\"card center\"><p><b>Steady load, badly sized pods?</b><br />→ VPA in <code>Off</code> → fix YAML, maybe <code>Initial</code></p></div>\n<div class=\"card center\"><p><b>Batch bursts, cost control?</b><br />→ CA with sane group min/max</p></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"callout co-warn\"><span class=\"ico\">⚠️</span><div><b>The two classic misconfigurations:</b> (1) HPA + VPA on the <b>same resource metric</b> — feedback war (CH 08). (2) HPA <code>minReplicas</code> higher than the cluster can host, with no CA — <b>permanent Pending</b> (Book 04 · CH 01's funnel, now self-inflicted by an autoscaler).</div></div>\n<div class=\"callout co-key\"><span class=\"ico\">🔑</span><div><b>Remember the ladder:</b> <i>HPA counts copies · VPA sizes copies · CA buys the building floor they stand on</i> — pick per question, never stack two scalers on the same signal, and the whole stack runs on Book 02's honest <code>requests</code>.</div></div>\n<p>⏭️ Prove all of it with your hands — <a href=\"#lab1\">Part V: Labs</a></p>\n<div class=\"center\"><a href=\"#toc\">↑ back to top</a></div>\n<div class=\"pgfoot\"><span>📘 Book 06 · Higher-Level Workloads</span><span><a href=\"#ch09\">◀ prev</a> · <a href=\"#toc\">▤ TOC</a> · <a href=\"#lab1\">labs ▶</a></span><span>Page 12</span></div></div>\n\n\n<div class=\"page\"><div class=\"pghead\"><span class=\"chip\">LAB 1</span><h2 id=\"daemonset-on-every-node\">🔬 DaemonSet on Every Node</h2><span class=\"dbadge\">🟠 12 MIN · HANDS-ON</span></div>\n<div class=\"labstep\"><div>STEP 1 · Deploy an agent — and feel the control-plane taint</div>\n<div class=\"term mini\"><span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl create ds agent --image=busybox:1.36 \\\n  -- sh -c <span class=\"m\">'sleep 9999'</span>\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl get ds agent\n<span class=\"y\">NAME   DESIRED  CURRENT  READY</span>\nagent  <span class=\"r\">0</span>        0        0  <span class=\"g\"># ZERO?! single control-plane node,\n# no toleration → runs NOWHERE (CH 02's trap!)</span></div></div>\n<div class=\"labstep\"><div>STEP 2 · Add the toleration — it appears</div>\n<div class=\"term mini\"><span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl patch ds agent <span class=\"y\">--type</span>=merge <span class=\"y\">-p</span> \\\n  <span class=\"m\">'{\"spec\":{\"template\":{\"spec\":{\"tolerations\":[{\"key\":\n  \"node-role.kubernetes.io/control-plane\",\"operator\":\"Exists\",\n  \"effect\":\"NoSchedule\"}]}}}}'</span>\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl get ds agent\n<span class=\"y\">NAME   DESIRED  CURRENT  READY  NODE SELECTOR</span>\nagent  <span class=\"p\">1</span>         1        1      &lt;none&gt; <span class=\"g\"># one per node — minikube has one node</span></div></div>\n<div class=\"grid2\">\n<div class=\"tabwin\"><div class=\"tabhead\">👀 LIMIT TO A SUBSET</div><div class=\"tabbody\"><span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl patch ds agent <span class=\"y\">--type</span>=merge <span class=\"y\">-p</span> \\\n  <span class=\"m\">'{\"spec\":{\"template\":{\"spec\":{\"nodeSelector\":\n  {\"role\":\"gpu\"}}}}}'</span>\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl get ds agent\n<span class=\"y\">DESIRED</span>\n<span class=\"r\">0</span>  <span class=\"g\"># no node has role=gpu —\n# \"1 per MATCHING node\" (CH 02)</span></div></div>\n<div class=\"tabwin\"><div class=\"tabhead\">🔍 ROLL IT</div><div class=\"tabbody\"><span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl set image ds/agent \\\n  busybox=busybox:1.36-musl\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl rollout status ds/agent\n<span class=\"p\">successfully rolled out</span>\n<span class=\"g\"># same machinery as deployments,\n# node by node (CH 02)</span></div></div>\n</div>\n<p><b>Proved:</b> DaemonSets count nodes, auto-tolerate nothing for the control plane, honor nodeSelector, and roll like Deployments. <b>Teardown:</b> <code>kubectl delete ds agent</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"center\"><a href=\"#toc\">↑ back to top</a></div>\n<div class=\"pgfoot\"><span>📘 Book 06 · Higher-Level Workloads</span><span><a href=\"#ch10\">◀ prev</a> · <a href=\"#toc\">▤ TOC</a> · <a href=\"#lab2\">next ▶</a></span><span>Page 13</span></div></div>\n\n\n<div class=\"page\"><div class=\"pghead\"><span class=\"chip\">LAB 2</span><h2 id=\"jobs-amp-a-manual-cronjob-trigger\">🔬 Jobs &amp; a Manual CronJob Trigger</h2><span class=\"dbadge\">🟠 10 MIN · HANDS-ON</span></div>\n<div class=\"labstep\"><div>STEP 1 · A counted Job — 4 successes, 2 at a time</div>\n<div class=\"term mini\"><span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl create job counted --image=busybox:1.36 \\\n  -- sh -c <span class=\"m\">'echo working; sleep 5'</span>\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl patch job counted <span class=\"y\">--type</span>=merge <span class=\"y\">-p</span> \\\n  <span class=\"m\">'{\"spec\":{\"completions\":4,\"parallelism\":2}}'</span>\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl get job counted -w\n<span class=\"y\">NAME     COMPLETIONS</span>\ncounted  <span class=\"p\">4/4</span>  <span class=\"g\"># successes counted — pods came and went</span>\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl get pods | <span class=\"c\">grep</span> counted\n<span class=\"g\">(pods remain as history — Completed; that's what TTL is for)</span></div></div>\n<div class=\"grid2\">\n<div class=\"tabwin\"><div class=\"tabhead\">💥 FAILURE PATH</div><div class=\"tabbody\"><span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl create job broken \\\n  --image=busybox:1.36 \\\n  -- sh -c <span class=\"m\">'exit 1'</span>\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl get job broken -w\n<span class=\"y\">COMPLETIONS  DURATION  AGE</span>\n0/1                  30s\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl describe job broken | tail -1\n<span class=\"r\">Job has reached the\nspecified backoff limit\n(default 6)</span>\n<span class=\"g\"># 6 failed pods → JOB failed.\n# backoffLimit in action</span></div></div>\n<div class=\"tabwin\"><div class=\"tabhead\">🗓️ CRONJOB, FIRED BY HAND</div><div class=\"tabbody\"><span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl create cronjob ticker \\\n  --image=busybox:1.36 \\\n  --schedule=<span class=\"m\">\"*/1 * * * *\"</span> \\\n  -- sh -c <span class=\"m\">'date'</span>\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl create job tick-now \\\n  <span class=\"y\">--from</span>=cronjob/ticker\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl get jobs\n<span class=\"y\">tick-now  1/1  Complete</span>\n<span class=\"g\"># schedule skipped —\n# same machinery, on demand</span></div></div>\n</div>\n<p><b>Proved:</b> completions/parallelism counting, backoffLimit killing a hopeless Job, and the <code>--from=cronjob/</code> test trigger. <b>Teardown:</b> <code>kubectl delete job counted broken tick-now; kubectl delete cronjob ticker</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"center\"><a href=\"#toc\">↑ back to top</a></div>\n<div class=\"pgfoot\"><span>📘 Book 06 · Higher-Level Workloads</span><span><a href=\"#lab1\">◀ prev</a> · <a href=\"#toc\">▤ TOC</a> · <a href=\"#lab3\">next ▶</a></span><span>Page 14</span></div></div>\n\n\n<div class=\"page\"><div class=\"pghead\"><span class=\"chip\">LAB 3</span><h2 id=\"hpa-watch-it-scale-under-load\">📈 HPA — Watch It Scale Under Load</h2><span class=\"dbadge\">🟠 15 MIN · HANDS-ON</span></div>\n<div class=\"labstep\"><div>STEP 1 · Metrics-server + a burner deployment</div>\n<div class=\"term mini\"><span class=\"p\">$</span> minikube addons enable metrics-server\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl top nodes  <span class=\"g\"># wait ~1 min — proves the pipeline works</span>\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl create deploy burner --image=polinux/stress \\\n  -- stress --cpu 1 --timeout 900s\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl set resources deploy burner <span class=\"y\">--requests</span>=cpu=<span class=\"y\">100m</span>\n<span class=\"g\"># request 100m, burns 1000m → 1000% utilization</span></div></div>\n<div class=\"labstep\"><div>STEP 2 · Arm the HPA — target 50%</div>\n<div class=\"term mini\"><span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl autoscale deploy burner <span class=\"y\">--min</span>=1 <span class=\"y\">--max</span>=<span class=\"y\">6</span> <span class=\"y\">--cpu-percent</span>=<span class=\"y\">50</span>\nhorizontalpodautoscaler.autoscaling/burner autoscaled\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl get hpa burner -w\n<span class=\"y\">NAME    REFERENCE         TARGETS   REPLICAS</span>\nburner  Deployment/burner  <span class=\"r\">1030%/50%</span>  1  <span class=\"g\"># usage vs REQUEST (CH 07!)</span>\nburner  Deployment/burner  1030%/50%  <span class=\"p\">6</span>  <span class=\"g\"># ceil(1 × 1030/50) = 21 → clamped to max 6</span></div></div>\n<div class=\"grid2\">\n<div class=\"tabwin\"><div class=\"tabhead\">👀 WATCH THE MATH</div><div class=\"tabbody\"><span class=\"g\"># each pod still burns 1000%\n# of its 100m request →\n# with 6 pods, avg ≈ 1000%\n# desired = ceil(6 × 20) = 120\n# → stays pinned at max 6.\n# THE CEILING HOLDS (wallet rail)</span></div></div>\n<div class=\"tabwin\"><div class=\"tabhead\">📉 COOL-DOWN (slow down!)</div><div class=\"tabbody\"><span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl delete deploy burner <span class=\"g\"># or wait out the 900s</span>\n<span class=\"g\"># on real cool-down: scale-DOWN\n# waits ~5 min (stabilization\n# window) — CH 07's asymmetry,\n# protecting against spikes</span></div></div>\n</div>\n<p><b>Proved:</b> utilization is measured against <code>requests</code>; the formula overshoots and clamps at <code>maxReplicas</code>; metrics-server feeds it all. <b>Teardown:</b> <code>kubectl delete hpa burner; kubectl delete deploy burner</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"center\"><a href=\"#toc\">↑ back to top</a></div>\n<div class=\"pgfoot\"><span>📘 Book 06 · Higher-Level Workloads</span><span><a href=\"#lab2\">◀ prev</a> · <a href=\"#toc\">▤ TOC</a> · <a href=\"#lab4\">next ▶</a></span><span>Page 15</span></div></div>\n\n\n<div class=\"page\"><div class=\"pghead\"><span class=\"chip\">LAB 4</span><h2 id=\"statefulset-partition-canary\">🔬 StatefulSet Partition Canary</h2><span class=\"dbadge\">🟠 12 MIN · HANDS-ON</span></div>\n<div class=\"labstep\"><div>STEP 1 · A 3-replica StatefulSet (Book 05 · Lab 3 pattern, condensed)</div>\n<div class=\"term mini\"><span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl create deploy web --image=nginx:1.25 --replicas=3 2&gt;/dev/null\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl delete deploy web 2&gt;/dev/null\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl apply -f - <span class=\"c\">&lt;&lt;EOF</span>\n<span class=\"c\">apiVersion</span>: apps/v1\n<span class=\"c\">kind</span>: StatefulSet\n<span class=\"c\">metadata</span>: { <span class=\"c\">name</span>: web }\n<span class=\"c\">spec</span>:\n  <span class=\"c\">serviceName</span>: web\n  <span class=\"c\">replicas</span>: <span class=\"y\">3</span>\n  <span class=\"c\">selector</span>: { <span class=\"c\">matchLabels</span>: { <span class=\"c\">app</span>: webs } }\n  <span class=\"c\">template</span>:\n    <span class=\"c\">metadata</span>: { <span class=\"c\">labels</span>: { <span class=\"c\">app</span>: webs } }\n    <span class=\"c\">spec</span>:\n      <span class=\"c\">containers</span>:\n      - { <span class=\"c\">name</span>: nginx, <span class=\"c\">image</span>: <span class=\"m\">nginx:1.25</span> }\n<span class=\"c\">EOF</span>\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl get sts web  <span class=\"g\"># READY 3/3 — ordered birth (CH 05)</span></div></div>\n<div class=\"labstep\"><div>STEP 2 · Set the partition BEFORE the new image</div>\n<div class=\"term mini\"><span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl patch sts web <span class=\"y\">--type</span>=merge <span class=\"y\">-p</span> \\\n  <span class=\"m\">'{\"spec\":{\"updateStrategy\":{\"rollingUpdate\":{\"partition\":2}}}}'</span>\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl set image sts/web nginx=<span class=\"y\">nginx:1.26</span>\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl get pods -o custom-columns=NAME:.metadata.name,IMAGE:.spec.containers[0].image\n<span class=\"y\">NAME   IMAGE</span>\nweb-0  nginx:<span class=\"r\">1.25</span>  <span class=\"g\"># frozen — ordinal &lt; partition</span>\nweb-1  nginx:<span class=\"r\">1.25</span>  <span class=\"g\"># frozen</span>\nweb-2  nginx:<span class=\"p\">1.26</span>  <span class=\"g\"># THE CANARY 🕊️</span></div></div>\n<div class=\"labstep\"><div>STEP 3 · Release — highest ordinal rolls first</div>\n<div class=\"term mini\"><span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl patch sts web <span class=\"y\">--type</span>=merge <span class=\"y\">-p</span> \\\n  <span class=\"m\">'{\"spec\":{\"updateStrategy\":{\"rollingUpdate\":{\"partition\":0}}}}'</span>\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl get pods -w\n<span class=\"g\"># web-1 replaces first, THEN web-0 — replicas before primary (CH 06)</span>\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl get pods -o custom-columns=NAME:.metadata.name,IMAGE:.spec.containers[0].image\n<span class=\"y\">web-0  nginx:1.26</span>  web-1  nginx:1.26  web-2  nginx:1.26  <span class=\"p\">✓</span></div></div>\n<p><b>Proved:</b> partition gates the rollout by ordinal; release = lowering the partition; direction is top-down. <b>Teardown:</b> <code>kubectl delete sts web</code> (no PVCs here — none were created).</p>\n<div class=\"center\"><a href=\"#toc\">↑ back to top</a></div>\n<div class=\"pgfoot\"><span>📘 Book 06 · Higher-Level Workloads</span><span><a href=\"#lab3\">◀ prev</a> · <a href=\"#toc\">▤ TOC</a> · <a href=\"#quiz\">quiz ▶</a></span><span>Page 16</span></div></div>\n\n\n<div class=\"page\"><div class=\"pghead\"><span class=\"chip\">QUIZ</span><h2 id=\"self-check-quiz\">✅ Self-Check Quiz</h2><span class=\"dbadge\">☑ 10 questions</span></div>\n<div class=\"qz\"><span class=\"qn\">Q1.</span>A DaemonSet's Pod count is determined by…<br /><b>A.</b> spec.replicas   <b>B.</b> the number of matching nodes   <b>C.</b> the HPA   <b>D.</b> the highest ordinal ever created</div>\n<div class=\"qz\"><span class=\"qn\">Q2.</span>Valid restartPolicy for a Job template?<br /><b>A.</b> Always   <b>B.</b> Always or Never   <b>C.</b> Never or OnFailure   <b>D.</b> none — Jobs don't restart</div>\n<div class=\"qz\"><span class=\"qn\">Q3.</span>CronJob with <code>concurrencyPolicy: Replace</code>, previous run still active, new tick fires:<br /><b>A.</b> old run is killed, new run starts   <b>B.</b> new tick is skipped   <b>C.</b> both run overlapped   <b>D.</b> CronJob suspends itself</div>\n<div class=\"qz\"><span class=\"qn\">Q4.</span>StatefulSet RollingUpdate with <code>partition: 2</code>, 3 replicas, image changed:<br /><b>A.</b> all pods update   <b>B.</b> only db-0 updates   <b>C.</b> nothing updates   <b>D.</b> only db-2 updates</div>\n<div class=\"qz\"><span class=\"qn\">Q5.</span>When a StatefulSet rollout completes (partition 0), the update order is…<br /><b>A.</b> db-0 → db-1 → db-2   <b>B.</b> db-2 → db-1 → db-0 (highest ordinal first)   <b>C.</b> random   <b>D.</b> all simultaneously</div>\n<div class=\"qz\"><span class=\"qn\">Q6.</span>An HPA with <code>type: Utilization</code> shows <code>unknown</code>. Most likely cause?<br /><b>A.</b> Pods lack resource <code>requests</code> (or metrics-server missing)   <b>B.</b> maxReplicas too low   <b>C.</b> wrong apiVersion   <b>D.</b> the Deployment is behind a Service</div>\n<div class=\"qz\"><span class=\"qn\">Q7.</span>DaemonSet Pods automatically tolerate which taints?<br /><b>A.</b> all taints including control-plane   <b>B.</b> none — explicit only   <b>C.</b> infrastructure conditions (not-ready, disk-pressure…) but NOT control-plane   <b>D.</b> only PreferNoSchedule</div>\n<div class=\"qz\"><span class=\"qn\">Q8.</span>The Cluster Autoscaler adds nodes primarily when…<br /><b>A.</b> CPU per node exceeds 80%   <b>B.</b> Pods are Pending because no node can fit them   <b>C.</b> the HPA hits maxReplicas   <b>D.</b> a node reports NotReady</div>\n<div class=\"qz\"><span class=\"qn\">Q9.</span>VPA in <code>Auto</code> mode applies new requests by…<br /><b>A.</b> editing the Deployment template in place, no restarts   <b>B.</b> only new pods   <b>C.</b> asking the HPA   <b>D.</b> evicting Pods so replacements start with the recommended size</div>\n<div class=\"qz\"><span class=\"qn\">Q10.</span>HPA + Cluster Autoscaler together:<br /><b>A.</b> conflict — choose one   <b>B.</b> both manage replicas   <b>C.</b> compose — HPA creates more Pods, CA adds nodes to fit them   <b>D.</b> only work on StatefulSets</div>\n<div class=\"center\"><a href=\"#toc\">↑ back to top</a></div>\n<div class=\"pgfoot\"><span>📘 Book 06 · Higher-Level Workloads</span><span><a href=\"#lab4\">◀ prev</a> · <a href=\"#toc\">▤ TOC</a> · <a href=\"#key\">answers ▶</a></span><span>Page 17</span></div></div>\n\n\n<div class=\"page\"><div class=\"pghead\"><span class=\"chip\">KEY</span><h2 id=\"answer-key-scoring\">🗝️ Answer Key + Scoring</h2><span class=\"dbadge\">grade yourself</span></div>\n<div class=\"table-scroll\"><table>\n<tr><th>Q</th><th>Ans</th><th>Why — one line</th></tr>\n<tr><td>1</td><td><b>B</b></td><td>No replicas field — the (matching) node list decides — CH 01</td></tr>\n<tr><td>2</td><td><b>C</b></td><td>Always is illegal for run-to-completion work — CH 03</td></tr>\n<tr><td>3</td><td><b>A</b></td><td>Replace = kill old, start new; Forbid skips; Allow overlaps — CH 04</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4</td><td><b>D</b></td><td>Partition gates by ordinal: only pods ≥ partition update — CH 06</td></tr>\n<tr><td>5</td><td><b>B</b></td><td>Highest-ordinal-first — followers before the primary — CH 06</td></tr>\n<tr><td>6</td><td><b>A</b></td><td>Utilization = usage ÷ request; missing pieces → unknown — CH 07</td></tr>\n<tr><td>7</td><td><b>C</b></td><td>Infrastructure taints auto; control-plane is opt-in — CH 02, Lab 1</td></tr>\n<tr><td>8</td><td><b>B</b></td><td>Pending-for-no-room is the buy signal — CH 09</td></tr>\n<tr><td>9</td><td><b>D</b></td><td>requests can't be edited live — evict &amp; recreate — CH 08</td></tr>\n<tr><td>10</td><td><b>C</b></td><td>Different layers: replicas (HPA) vs nodes (CA) — CH 10</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"grid3\">\n<div class=\"card center\"><div>🏆</div><p><b>9–10</b><br />Ready for Book 07</p></div>\n<div class=\"card center\"><div>📖</div><p><b>6–8</b><br />Re-read missed chapters' 🔑 boxes</p></div>\n<div class=\"card center\"><div>🔁</div><p><b>&lt;6</b><br />Re-run Labs 1–4, then retake</p></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"callout co-tip\"><span class=\"ico\">💡</span><div><b>Missed Q4/Q5?</b> Partition + roll direction is <i>the</i> StatefulSet update mental model — canary from the top down. Missed Q6? HPA without <code>requests</code> is the #1 \"why won't it scale\" ticket in the wild.</div></div>\n<div class=\"center\"><a href=\"#toc\">↑ back to top</a></div>\n<div class=\"pgfoot\"><span>📘 Book 06 · Higher-Level Workloads</span><span><a href=\"#quiz\">◀ prev</a> · <a href=\"#toc\">▤ TOC</a> · <a href=\"#gloss\">next ▶</a></span><span>Page 18</span></div></div>\n\n\n<div class=\"page\"><div class=\"pghead\"><span class=\"chip\">GLOSS</span><h2 id=\"glossary\">📚 Glossary</h2><span class=\"dbadge\">🔵 REFERENCE</span></div>\n<div class=\"gl\"><b>DaemonSet</b> — one Pod per matching node; node joins spawn, node leaves collect; agent workloads (logs, metrics, CNI, CSI node plugins).</div>\n<div class=\"gl\"><b>updateStrategy (DS)</b> — RollingUpdate (maxUnavailable; no maxSurge) or OnDelete.</div>\n<div class=\"gl\"><b>Job</b> — run-to-completion workload: completions, parallelism, backoffLimit, activeDeadlineSeconds, ttlSecondsAfterFinished, completionMode Indexed.</div>\n<div class=\"gl\"><b>CronJob</b> — schedule + Job template; concurrencyPolicy (Allow/Forbid/Replace), startingDeadlineSeconds, suspend, timeZone.</div>\n<div class=\"gl\"><b>StatefulSet</b> — ordered lifecycle, stable names/DNS, per-replica storage (Book 05); podManagementPolicy OrderedReady/Parallel.</div>\n<div class=\"gl\"><b>partition</b> — StatefulSet canary gate: only ordinals ≥ partition update; roll direction highest-first.</div>\n<div class=\"gl\"><b>OnDelete</b> — update strategy: template applies only when you delete each Pod manually.</div>\n<div class=\"gl\"><b>HorizontalPodAutoscaler</b> — scales replicas from metrics; v2 API; needs metrics-server + Pod requests; min/max rails; fast up, slow down (stabilization window).</div>\n<div class=\"gl\"><b>Utilization</b> — actual usage ÷ resource request; the default HPA metric basis.</div>\n<div class=\"gl\"><b>VerticalPodAutoscaler</b> — recommends/applies requests+limits; modes Off / Initial / Auto(Recreate); conflicts with HPA on the same metric.</div>\n<div class=\"gl\"><b>Cluster Autoscaler</b> — node-count automation: adds nodes for Pending Pods, removes underutilized nodes ~10 min; respects PDBs, local storage (safe-to-evict annotation), priority.</div>\n<div class=\"gl\"><b>metrics-server</b> — the in-cluster usage pipeline (kubectl top, HPA Resource metrics).</div>\n<div class=\"gl\"><b>ttlSecondsAfterFinished</b> — automatic cleanup age for finished Jobs.</div>\n<div class=\"gl\"><b>JOB_COMPLETION_INDEX</b> — env var in Indexed Jobs for sharded work queues.</div>\n<div class=\"center\"><a href=\"#toc\">↑ back to top</a></div>\n<div class=\"pgfoot\"><span>📘 Book 06 · Higher-Level Workloads</span><span><a href=\"#key\">◀ prev</a> · <a href=\"#toc\">▤ TOC</a> · <a href=\"#cheat\">next ▶</a></span><span>Page 19</span></div></div>\n\n\n<div class=\"page\"><div class=\"pghead\"><span class=\"chip\">CHEAT</span><h2 id=\"one-page-cheat-sheet\">📄 One-Page Cheat Sheet</h2><span class=\"dbadge\">🔵 print me</span></div>\n<div class=\"grid2\">\n<div class=\"card\"><div class=\"zlabel\">🦾 Workloads — commands</div><div class=\"term mini\"><span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl get ds,job,cronjob,hpa\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl create job test --from=cronjob/x\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl set image ds/agent img=v2\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl rollout status ds/agent\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl autoscale deploy web --min=2 --max=10 --cpu-percent=60\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl get hpa -w\n<span class=\"p\">$</span> kubectl top pods <span class=\"g\"># needs metrics-server</span></div></div>\n<div class=\"card\"><div class=\"zlabel\">🕊️ STS canary pattern</div><div class=\"term mini\"><span class=\"c\">updateStrategy</span>:\n  <span class=\"c\">rollingUpdate</span>: { <span class=\"c\">partition</span>: <span class=\"y\">N-1</span> }\n<span class=\"g\"># set image → top pod only</span>\n<span class=\"g\"># verify → lower partition</span>\n2 → 1 → 0\n<span class=\"g\"># roll = highest ordinal first\n# (replicas before primary)</span></div></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"grid2\">\n<div class=\"card\"><div class=\"zlabel\">🧩 Scaler chooser</div><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Scaler</th></tr><tr><td>load spikes, pods pegged</td><td>HPA (replicas)</td></tr><tr><td>pods sized wrong, steady</td><td>VPA (requests)</td></tr><tr><td>nothing fits, Pending</td><td>Cluster Autoscaler (nodes)</td></tr><tr><td>HPA + VPA same metric</td><td>❌ feedback war — split signals</td></tr></table></div></div>\n<div class=\"card\"><div class=\"zlabel\">📌 Field quick-ref</div><div class=\"term mini\"><span class=\"g\">Job:</span> completions · parallelism ·\n  backoffLimit · activeDeadlineSeconds ·\n  ttlSecondsAfterFinished · restartPolicy Never/OnFailure\n<span class=\"g\">CronJob:</span> schedule · concurrencyPolicy\n  (Forbid for backups!) · startingDeadlineSeconds\n<span class=\"g\">HPA math:</span> ceil(replicas × used/target)\n  ±10% tolerance · clamped min/max</div></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card\"><div class=\"zlabel\">🧠 Facts worth a job offer</div>\n<ul>\n<li>DaemonSet: node list = replica count; auto-tolerates infra taints but NOT control-plane; drain skips its Pods</li>\n<li>Jobs count successes and bound failures — restartPolicy must be Never/OnFailure; CronJob's real decision is Allow vs Forbid vs Replace</li>\n<li>StatefulSet rollouts: highest-ordinal-first; partition = graduated canary, frozen while partition = replicas</li>\n<li>HPA needs requests + metrics-server; utilization = usage ÷ request; fast up, 5-min-stabilized down</li>\n<li>VPA right-sizes by eviction; HPA+VPA on the same metric = war — use custom metrics + resources instead</li>\n<li>CA buys nodes for Pending Pods and sells idle ones — PDBs, local storage, and priority are its fences</li>\n</ul></div>\n<div class=\"center\"><a href=\"#toc\">↑ back to top</a></div>\n<div class=\"pgfoot\"><span>📘 Book 06 · Higher-Level Workloads</span><span><a href=\"#gloss\">◀ prev</a> · <a href=\"#toc\">▤ TOC</a> · <a href=\"#finale\">finale ▶</a></span><span>Page 20</span></div></div>\n\n\n<div class=\"page\"><div class=\"pghead\"><span class=\"chip\">FINALE</span><h2 id=\"what-you-can-do-now\">🗺️ What You Can Do Now</h2><span class=\"dbadge\">🎓 Book 06 complete</span></div>\n<p>Books 01–05 built, dressed, connected, placed, and persisted your workloads — Book 06 <b>completed the zoo and taught it to run itself</b>.</p>\n<div class=\"mtree\"><b>🦾 THE FULL WORKLOAD ZOO:</b>\n├── <u>Deployment</u>     <span class=\"g\">stateless replicas · rolling + undo (Book 01)</span>\n├── <u>DaemonSet</u>      <span class=\"g\">agent per node · node list = count</span>\n├── <u>Job / CronJob</u>  <span class=\"g\">run-to-done · schedules · concurrency policies</span>\n├── <u>StatefulSet</u>    <span class=\"g\">identity + storage + ORDERED + partition canaries</span>\n└── <u>Autoscaling</u>    <span class=\"g\">HPA (count) · VPA (size) · CA (nodes) — a stack</span></div>\n<h3 id=\"you-can-now\">✅ You can now…</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Ship node agents as DaemonSets — and explain why your log collector and CNI had no choice</li>\n<li>Run batch work with real failure semantics, and schedule backups that can't overlap themselves to death</li>\n<li>Roll database images with partition canaries — one replica verified before the primary ever moves</li>\n<li>Wire an HPA the right way (requests + metrics-server) and predict its replica math</li>\n<li>Choose among HPA/VPA/CA per question, and stack them without feedback wars</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"callout co-key\"><span class=\"ico\">🎓</span><div><b>Where to next — Book 07 · Observability &amp; Operations:</b> your workloads now scale themselves — but <i>how do you know they're healthy?</i> Probes (the hole Book 01 flagged), Metrics Server &amp; <code>kubectl top</code>, Prometheus + Grafana, logging architecture, and cluster-scope debugging. Your own Loki/Prometheus/Grafana stack maps straight onto it — now you'll see the whole discipline from the Kubernetes side.</div></div>\n<div class=\"center\">— End of Book 06 · 🎬 —</div>\n<div class=\"pgfoot\"><span>📘 Book 06 · Higher-Level Workloads</span><span><a href=\"#cheat\">◀ prev</a> · <a href=\"#toc\">▤ TOC</a></span><span>Page 21</span></div></div>\n\n\n","toc":[{"id":"higher-levelworkloads","text":"HIGHER-LEVELWORKLOADS","level":1},{"id":"contents-click-any-row","text":"Contents — click any row","level":2},{"id":"daemonset-one-pod-per-node","text":"📡 DaemonSet — One Pod Per Node","level":2},{"id":"daemonset-updates-amp-node-lifecycle","text":"🔄 DaemonSet — Updates &amp; Node Lifecycle","level":2},{"id":"node-churn-the-automatic-part","text":"🆕 Node churn — the automatic part","level":3},{"id":"updatestrategy-rolling-your-agents","text":"🎞️ updateStrategy — rolling your agents","level":3},{"id":"jobs-run-to-completion","text":"⏳ Jobs — Run to Completion","level":2},{"id":"cronjobs-schedules-amp-concurrency","text":"🗓️ CronJobs — Schedules &amp; Concurrency","level":2},{"id":"statefulsets-ordered-lifecycle-amp-identity","text":"🪪 StatefulSets — Ordered Lifecycle &amp; Identity","level":2},{"id":"statefulset-updates-partition-canaries","text":"🕊️ StatefulSet Updates — Partition Canaries","level":2},{"id":"hpa-horizontal-pod-autoscaler","text":"📈 HPA — Horizontal Pod Autoscaler","level":2},{"id":"the-math-it-s-one-formula","text":"🧮 The math (it's one formula)","level":3},{"id":"vpa-vertical-autoscaler-overview","text":"📏 VPA — Vertical Autoscaler (Overview)","level":2},{"id":"cluster-autoscaler-nodes-on-demand","text":"🖥️ Cluster Autoscaler — Nodes on Demand","level":2},{"id":"the-trio-together-when-to-use-which","text":"🧩 The Trio Together — When to Use Which","level":2},{"id":"how-they-stack-the-beautiful-part","text":"🏗️ How they stack (the beautiful part)","level":3},{"id":"daemonset-on-every-node","text":"🔬 DaemonSet on Every Node","level":2},{"id":"jobs-amp-a-manual-cronjob-trigger","text":"🔬 Jobs &amp; a Manual CronJob Trigger","level":2},{"id":"hpa-watch-it-scale-under-load","text":"📈 HPA — Watch It Scale Under Load","level":2},{"id":"statefulset-partition-canary","text":"🔬 StatefulSet Partition Canary","level":2},{"id":"self-check-quiz","text":"✅ Self-Check Quiz","level":2},{"id":"answer-key-scoring","text":"🗝️ Answer Key + Scoring","level":2},{"id":"glossary","text":"📚 Glossary","level":2},{"id":"one-page-cheat-sheet","text":"📄 One-Page Cheat Sheet","level":2},{"id":"what-you-can-do-now","text":"🗺️ What You Can Do Now","level":2},{"id":"you-can-now","text":"✅ You can now…","level":3}],"words":5827,"assets":[]};